    "website": "https://alegriamontessori.com/",
    "content": "<p>Alegria Montessori School provides a traditional Montessori education for children ages 1 through 8th grade, with two beautiful campuses in Saint Petersburg, FL. The school serves 117 students with a 15:1 average class size and 9 classroom teachers, ensuring personalized attention for each child. With 50% of faculty holding advanced degrees, the school emphasizes quality instruction and individualized learning approaches.</p><p>Recognized for supporting students with mild learning differences, Alegria Montessori offers specialized learning programs designed to meet the needs of children who may require additional support in their educational journey. The school's nonsectarian environment and Montessori-based curriculum create a nurturing space where students can explore, learn, and grow at their own pace. Families seeking a structured yet flexible educational setting will find the school's approach particularly beneficial for children with learning differences.</p><p>Admissions are on a rolling basis, and the school offers financial aid to 10% of students, with an average grant of $5,600. Tuition ranges from $9,000 depending on age and program length. Alegria Montessori is accredited by the American Montessori Society (AMS) and provides a rich array of extracurricular activities including dance, soccer, swimming, art, music, and Spanish classes to support holistic development.</p>",
    "summary": "Alegria Montessori School in Saint Petersburg, Florida serves 117 students in grades Prekindergarten-8.",
